*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !OSWRITE(data, path)
*
* Writes DATA to the operating system file PATH with no change to a byte (no field mark is turned into a newline), replacing what
* the file held, which is cut to the length of DATA.  The file is made if it is not there.  STATUS() is 0 if it was written.
* The openQM ON ERROR clause is not supported: a failure is the STATUS() and not an abort.
*
* An ordinary program, not an internal one, as !OSREAD is: the OPENSEQ in it asks the OS-access gate of the account.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

subroutine !oswrite(data, path)
$catalog !oswrite

   if path = '' then return

   * The ELSE of OPENSEQ is a file that was not there as well as a failure; the STATUS() says which (0 for a file that is made).
   * A failure leaves the STATUS() it made: this is not an internal program and cannot SET.STATUS, so nothing is done after the
   * failing statement that could change it (the file is left open until the program ends).
   openseq path overwrite to f then null else
      if status() # 0 then return
   end
   weofseq f
   writeblk data to f else return
   closeseq f
   return
end

* END-CODE
